  "title": "A clearer view of community models",
  "summary": "Model discovery got sharper, the CLI learned to find voices, and several generation and account flows became less surprising.\n\nModel Monitor now puts community-model Trust scores beside Health, with a sortable comparison to the official models they are named after. The catalog marks official Pollinations agents, model-list category filters return matching results, and health data separates Pollen-related 402 responses from other 4xx errors. Empty text answers now count against community-model discovery health. Model display titles were also cleaned up without changing their IDs or routing. A GPT-6.1 Terra registry entry was merged with its release date still TBD.\n\n`polli models` gained search, source and reliability filters, plus `--voices` for finding voices by audio model. The CLI now honors `POLLINATIONS_API_KEY` ahead of stored credentials, and its npm-backed client commands work on Windows. The BYOP guide gained a Python device-flow example, while API docs corrected the OpenAI SDK base URL and refreshed model-health and model-list information.\n\nGemini tool calls now accept and return Google's thought-signature format across streamed and non-streamed chat. Claude Code tool-search results and mid-conversation tool changes are accepted on `/v1/messages`. Multipart image edits pass through their seed, Wan 2.2 fast selects a supported ratio from the start image, and prompt-agent updates identify invalid fields and base models earlier. Successful empty chat streams can also receive cache hits on repeat requests.",
